00:48:25.830 --> 00:48:29.890
And I remember being totally like, oh, oh, wow.

937
00:48:30.110 --> 00:48:30.590
OK.

938
00:48:30.890 --> 00:48:34.950
Of course, Kevin says this is the best meeting they've ever had.

939
00:48:35.110 --> 00:48:35.770
The best one.

940
00:48:35.930 --> 00:48:41.650
If you guys get a chance and rewatch the scene at the end, Toby takes away the Kama Sutra.

941
00:48:41.810 --> 00:48:46.330
And I want you to look at Phyllis's face because she makes an expression like she's really bummed

942
00:48:46.330 --> 00:48:47.290
out to lose the book.

943
00:48:48.330 --> 00:48:49.330
Oh, my gosh.

944
00:48:49.330 --> 00:48:50.330
I missed that.

945
00:48:51.530 --> 00:48:53.690
Oh, I can't wait to go back and see that.

946
00:48:53.870 --> 00:48:54.010
Yeah.

947
00:48:54.250 --> 00:48:57.470
Well, Angela, should we talk a little bit about what's going on in Stanford?

948
00:48:57.670 --> 00:49:03.050
You mean with Josh Porter's like biker shorts and his fancy bike and Jim and his clunky

949
00:49:03.050 --> 00:49:04.830
bike with a big basket?

950
00:49:05.010 --> 00:49:05.970
What's happening, Jim?

951
00:49:06.190 --> 00:49:07.090
What's going on?

952
00:49:07.330 --> 00:49:10.770
Well, Jim has started biking to work just like Josh.

953
00:49:11.070 --> 00:49:13.350
He says, I'm going to save gas money.

954
00:49:13.350 --> 00:49:14.670
It keeps me in shape.

955
00:49:15.190 --> 00:49:18.270
He did not anticipate how sweaty he would be.

956
00:49:18.430 --> 00:49:22.090
That talking head is so funny how much sweat they put on him.

957
00:49:22.290 --> 00:49:26.310
Angela, do you remember how they used to make us sweaty when you have to be sweaty?

958
00:49:26.490 --> 00:49:27.630
They spray you.

959
00:49:27.810 --> 00:49:32.890
Yeah, they would either spray you with like a bottle that you would mist your plants with

960
00:49:33.370 --> 00:49:39.670
or they would spray you with like those Evian mist sprays and they have to like spritz

961
00:49:39.670 --> 00:49:45.010
you under the arms, but then they'd have to come and do it like between every take because

962
00:49:45.010 --> 00:49:45.750
it would dry.

963
00:49:45.970 --> 00:49:51.850
But then sometimes they would put like baby oil around like your hairline and then spray

964
00:49:51.850 --> 00:49:54.090
you so it would look especially sweaty.

965
00:49:54.670 --> 00:49:59.170
I've just given everybody a little inside info on how you make an actor sweaty.

966
00:49:59.430 --> 00:50:00.830
You can try it at home.

967
00:50:01.570 --> 00:50:05.470
Jenna, I'm just laughing at how many times you just said sweaty.

968
00:50:05.890 --> 00:50:06.410
Sweaty.

969
00:50:08.330 --> 00:50:09.210
All right.

970
00:50:09.410 --> 00:50:15.390
So now at four minutes, 23 seconds, Sam, will you play Mustang?

971
00:50:16.070 --> 00:50:17.070
Flirty Karen.

972
00:50:17.270 --> 00:50:18.310
Flirty Karen.

973
00:50:18.310 --> 00:50:20.190
That's my mom, Birdie Kinsey.

974
00:50:20.390 --> 00:50:21.290
Flirty Karen.

975
00:50:21.890 --> 00:50:24.550
Karen says, hey, nice basket.

976
00:50:24.830 --> 00:50:27.430
Ever since the whole chips incident, she's smitten.

977
00:50:28.150 --> 00:50:28.410
Yep.

978
00:50:28.850 --> 00:50:35.010
So then Josh comes over and gives Karen the company credit card because they have to work

979
00:50:35.010 --> 00:50:37.510
late and they're allowed to buy dinner.

980
00:50:37.790 --> 00:50:41.850
But he says, you know, no more than $20 a person this time.

981
00:50:42.010 --> 00:50:44.410
This time, $20 a person.

982
00:50:44.630 --> 00:50:46.390
We shot this in 2006.

983
00:50:48.130 --> 00:50:52.370
Is there a meal out there that you order that's more than $20 a person?

984
00:50:52.610 --> 00:50:55.130
Hey, maybe there's a reason Stanford doesn't make it.

985
00:50:56.230 --> 00:50:57.610
I mean, my gosh.

986
00:50:58.790 --> 00:50:59.750
I don't know.

987
00:51:00.870 --> 00:51:04.370
Maybe I just don't eat at very fancy places for my takeout.

988
00:51:04.530 --> 00:51:11.750
But I feel like I would be challenged to order a meal for more than $20 a person in 2006.

989
00:51:12.070 --> 00:51:12.390
Yeah.

990
00:51:12.770 --> 00:51:15.390
Especially like late at night in Scranton.

991
00:51:15.530 --> 00:51:16.110
What are they getting?

992
00:51:16.470 --> 00:51:17.870
You know, like Thai food.

993
00:51:18.030 --> 00:51:18.550
I know.

994
00:51:18.990 --> 00:51:19.550
Exactly.

995
00:51:19.770 --> 00:51:20.630
This is not difficult.

996
00:51:21.510 --> 00:51:24.230
Andy, though, busts out some Jaegermeister.

997
00:51:24.230 --> 00:51:25.830
But he's got other plans.

998
00:51:26.030 --> 00:51:26.870
He's ready to party.

999
00:51:27.070 --> 00:51:33.270
Ed Helms' face when he holds up that Jaegermeister bottle and the shot glasses is hilarious.

1000
00:51:34.230 --> 00:51:37.890
You get a window into who Andy was in college and you're like, oh, buddy.

1001
00:51:38.330 --> 00:51:43.410
Well, back in Scranton, things are getting exciting because everyone is showing up to Diwali.

1002
00:51:43.930 --> 00:51:44.810
They're arriving.

1003
00:51:45.030 --> 00:51:45.810
They're walking in.

1004
00:51:45.950 --> 00:51:48.110
It's really, really like bright and colorful.

1005
00:51:48.110 --> 00:51:49.410
And there's music playing.

1006
00:51:49.650 --> 00:51:52.750
And Phyllis is like, isn't it fun to take our shoes off?

1007
00:51:52.750 --> 00:51:56.710
And Angela's like, I wish not everyone took their shoes off.

1008
00:51:56.830 --> 00:51:58.050
And Kevin's like, stop it.

1009
00:51:58.150 --> 00:51:59.630
I told you it was a condition.

1010
00:51:59.990 --> 00:52:08.890
So you guys remember in grief counseling, we talked about a deleted scene that would have been in the episode where Angela and Kevin go off again about his sweaty feet.

1011
00:52:09.090 --> 00:52:09.410
Yes.

1012
00:52:09.410 --> 00:52:11.890
This is a callback to a deleted scene.

1013
00:52:12.210 --> 00:52:16.150
So it's going to go unappreciated by most viewers.

1014
00:52:16.330 --> 00:52:20.010
But those diehard viewers who watch those deleted scenes will know what this means.

1015
00:52:20.050 --> 00:52:26.210
I feel like someone in the writer's room was really determined to make sure we had scenes about Kevin's feet.

1016
00:52:26.310 --> 00:52:30.710
I feel like it was a note card on the wall that said Kevin's sweaty feet.

1017
00:52:30.710 --> 00:52:34.690
And someone loved it and kept wanting to get it in the episodes.

1018
00:52:35.850 --> 00:52:37.830
Well, this is Angela's worst nightmare.

1019
00:52:38.090 --> 00:52:41.970
People taking off all their shoes, even minus Kevin's sweaty feet.

1020
00:52:42.030 --> 00:52:45.470
I mean, this is just not how she wants to be at a party.

1021
00:52:46.030 --> 00:52:47.230
No, no.

1022
00:52:47.590 --> 00:52:50.610
So, Angela, we got a fan question about these Diwali scenes.

1023
00:52:50.750 --> 00:52:52.110
It comes from Sarah Beth Miller.

1024
00:52:52.110 --> 00:52:57.350
She asked, was this a real Diwali celebration happening in the filming of this episode?

1025
00:52:57.690 --> 00:53:01.010
How did you get all of those people in those beautiful costumes?

1026
00:53:02.150 --> 00:53:03.750
Great question, Sarah Beth.

1027
00:53:04.070 --> 00:53:07.190
I mean, there are so many people in this scene.

1028
00:53:07.370 --> 00:53:08.530
So here's the thing.

1029
00:53:08.690 --> 00:53:10.610
It was not a real Diwali festival.

1030
00:53:11.130 --> 00:53:16.190
That was all put together by our amazing crew, just specifically for this episode.

1031
00:53:16.190 --> 00:53:22.090
Yes, our set designer, Michael Gallenberg, and his team, they decorated that whole gym.

1032
00:53:22.790 --> 00:53:29.150
Michael had to do a lot of research in order to transform the gymnasium to feel like a real Diwali festival.

1033
00:53:29.150 --> 00:53:33.010
So I think he would be very proud to know that you wondered if this was real.

1034
00:53:33.230 --> 00:53:36.410
Like, maybe we just stepped into an existing festival.

1035
00:53:36.650 --> 00:53:39.150
No, they made the whole thing.

1036
00:53:39.290 --> 00:53:40.470
They did a fantastic job.

1037
00:53:40.670 --> 00:53:44.590
As far as costumes go, my character did not get to dress up, Jenna.

1038
00:53:44.730 --> 00:53:45.610
I was so bummed.

1039
00:53:46.230 --> 00:53:46.630
Yeah.

1040
00:53:47.170 --> 00:53:49.770
I mean, she actually is just wearing what she wore to work.

1041
00:53:49.930 --> 00:53:51.990
She didn't even change out of her work clothes.

1042
00:53:52.170 --> 00:53:52.670
I know.

1043
00:53:52.930 --> 00:53:55.250
But some of the cast did get to dress up.

1044
00:53:55.410 --> 00:54:02.410
BJ, Rain, Mindy, and I'm sure our wardrobe stylist was thrilled to do something other than just drab office attire.

1045
00:54:02.670 --> 00:54:07.030
They used to get so excited every time we got to wear anything other than our office attire.

1046
00:54:07.170 --> 00:54:11.110
And Pam didn't really dress up, but she is not in her office attire, which was fun.

1047
00:54:11.190 --> 00:54:12.950
I had a whole separate fitting for that.

1048
00:54:13.150 --> 00:54:14.530
We got to see casual Pam.

1049
00:54:15.190 --> 00:54:17.830
And did you notice I got to wear my hair differently as well?

1050
00:54:17.930 --> 00:54:23.230
But we did find out some interesting trivia about all the other background actors who were dressed up for this festival.

1051
00:54:23.390 --> 00:54:23.630
Yes.

1052
00:54:23.810 --> 00:54:28.790
We went to Kentopedia, and he said our casting office worked with Central Casting.

1053
00:54:29.070 --> 00:54:31.990
Now, Central Casting is a casting agency in Los Angeles.

1054
00:54:31.990 --> 00:54:36.670
They specialize in sort of the background actors and filling out the picture, right?

1055
00:54:37.170 --> 00:54:37.310
Yeah.

1056
00:54:37.730 --> 00:54:43.110
But Central Casting reached out to a lot of the Indian community here in Los Angeles to hire those background players.

1057
00:54:43.110 --> 00:54:53.010
All in all, Kent said we had 100 extras working this episode, and every single one of them brought their own very beautiful costuming for us to use.

1058
00:54:53.010 --> 00:55:01.470
And to kind of fill out the world, Kent also hired a professional dance company to come and lead us in some of the dances.

1059
00:55:01.470 --> 00:55:08.490
He found a company called NDM Dance Productions, and he hired their director choreographer, Dev Mahajan.

1060
00:55:08.670 --> 00:55:11.070
And Dev hired eight dancers.

1061
00:55:11.310 --> 00:55:18.150
He choreographed, rehearsed their dance in the morning of that day four of shooting is when we shot all the dancing.

1062
00:55:18.150 --> 00:55:24.450
And then we filmed it later in the afternoon, and all the dancers wear their own costumes as well.

1063
00:55:24.650 --> 00:55:26.550
I actually went to the website.

1064
00:55:26.830 --> 00:55:27.710
Of course you did, lady.

1065
00:55:27.830 --> 00:55:29.130
You went to the dancer's website.

1066
00:55:29.230 --> 00:55:29.850
What'd you find out?

1067
00:55:29.950 --> 00:55:31.910
They have appeared on tons of shows.

1068
00:55:32.130 --> 00:55:42.130
So You Think You Can Dance, eLive Oscar coverage, Good Morning America, Superstars of Dance, and MTV's America's Best Dance Crew.

1069
00:55:42.130 --> 00:55:46.930
If you want to look them up, you can find them at ndmdance.com.

1070
00:55:47.090 --> 00:55:53.270
It was super cool, and it really did end up feeling like a real party, like a real celebration.

1071
00:55:53.550 --> 00:55:54.470
It really did.

1072
00:55:54.470 --> 00:56:02.130
I wish my character wanted to participate more because me, Angela, that is me, would have been right out there, like, just having a great time.

1073
00:56:02.150 --> 00:56:09.430
So it was always hard in these moments to not get to be in costume and not participate and be kind of the grump on the wall, you know?

1074
00:56:09.430 --> 00:56:16.410
Well, I do, and we'll talk a little bit about my dancing later, but I did get to dance a little bit, and I was thrilled.

1075
00:56:16.710 --> 00:56:17.010
Yes.

1076
00:56:17.010 --> 00:56:17.470
Very fun.

1077
00:56:17.790 --> 00:56:21.450
All right, so yeah, so there are people that got to dress up, people that didn't.

1078
00:56:21.650 --> 00:56:27.070
Michael and Carol walk in with a whole different idea of what this party is.

1079
00:56:27.290 --> 00:56:33.030
Michael has clearly told Carol that this is a costume party, so she arrives dressed as a cheerleader.

1080
00:56:33.250 --> 00:56:34.790
With pom-poMs.

1081
00:56:35.150 --> 00:56:36.290
With pom-poMs.

1082
00:56:36.290 --> 00:56:39.630
And Michael has his old Halloween costume on.

1083
00:56:39.730 --> 00:56:41.450
He has his papier-mâché head.

1084
00:56:41.890 --> 00:56:44.550
We had a fan question from Melinda O'Brien.

1085
00:56:44.810 --> 00:56:49.950
Was Michael's costume the same one from the Halloween episode, or did they have to make another one?

1086
00:56:50.110 --> 00:56:52.310
Oh, no, Melinda, we save everything.

1087
00:56:52.850 --> 00:56:59.230
Everything that anyone wore or held or used or interacted with on The Office goes into a giant warehouse.

1088
00:56:59.230 --> 00:57:00.150
It's tagged.

1089
00:57:00.330 --> 00:57:01.770
It's almost like an evidence room.

1090
00:57:01.770 --> 00:57:09.190
So when they wrote that into this episode, they just went to that warehouse, and they picked up that papier-mâché head and put it right on his shoulder again.

1091
00:57:09.490 --> 00:57:09.950
That's right.

1092
00:57:09.950 --> 00:57:11.950
It's like the end of Raiders of the Lost Ark.

1093
00:57:12.150 --> 00:57:16.150
It's like rows and rows of boxes with dates, tags, episode names.

1094
00:57:16.390 --> 00:57:18.030
So they went right to that box.

1095
00:57:18.170 --> 00:57:22.870
And, of course, Michael, you know, he can take the head off, and then he just looks like he's in a suit.

1096
00:57:22.870 --> 00:57:28.610
But Carol is stuck now as a cheerleader because Michael thought this was Indian Halloween.

1097
00:57:29.570 --> 00:57:30.690
Yes, I know.

1098
00:57:30.910 --> 00:57:31.690
Poor Carol.

1099
00:57:31.930 --> 00:57:35.510
She is such a sport in this episode.

1100
00:57:35.530 --> 00:57:37.270
She has to endure so much.

1101
00:57:37.450 --> 00:57:40.650
And Nancy Carell just knocked it out of the park.

1102
00:57:40.870 --> 00:57:46.010
She plays it so perfect of just sort of, like, quietly enduring this awkward evening.

1103
00:57:46.890 --> 00:57:48.610
While dressed like a cheerleader.

1104
00:57:48.790 --> 00:57:49.030
Yeah.

1105
00:57:49.670 --> 00:57:51.630
Well, let's move over to the buffet.

1106
00:57:53.090 --> 00:57:54.110
Angela's at the buffet.

1107
00:57:54.450 --> 00:57:57.250
She asks if they have any vegetarian options.

1108
00:57:58.310 --> 00:58:02.710
She doesn't even seem satisfied when she learns that everything is vegetarian.

1109
00:58:02.950 --> 00:58:04.050
It's all vegetarian.

1110
00:58:04.070 --> 00:58:05.890
She's just in full grump mode.

1111
00:58:05.970 --> 00:58:07.510
She's like, just give me some bread.

1112
00:58:08.050 --> 00:58:11.790
And then the guy hands her the bread with his hands.

1113
00:58:11.970 --> 00:58:15.510
And, Angela, you have a line here that I am fairly certain you improvised.

1114
00:58:15.690 --> 00:58:16.130
Oh, yeah.

1115
00:58:16.130 --> 00:58:20.010
I say, you used your hands as I walk away.

1116
00:58:20.270 --> 00:58:25.450
And I did improvise that because the guy literally did hand it to me with his hands.

1117
00:58:25.610 --> 00:58:28.970
And I thought, that's not good.

1118
00:58:29.490 --> 00:58:31.170
You should have used some tongs.

1119
00:58:31.290 --> 00:58:32.170
Some tongs.

1120
00:58:32.190 --> 00:58:33.450
He just handed it to me with his hands.

1121
00:58:33.570 --> 00:58:36.950
And so I improvised that line and it stayed in and it makes me laugh.

1122
00:58:37.070 --> 00:58:38.810
Of course, she goes ahead and eats it.

1123
00:58:38.930 --> 00:58:40.470
So I guess she's not too concerned.

1124
00:58:40.470 --> 00:58:44.370
But it's clearly she's just like not having a good time.

1125
00:58:44.550 --> 00:58:48.410
And she's a little like grossed out because she's seeing a lot of feet.

1126
00:58:48.770 --> 00:58:51.510
And now a guy just handed her bread with his hands.

1127
00:58:51.670 --> 00:58:52.150
A stranger.

1128
00:58:52.430 --> 00:58:57.030
Well, in the script, it says that you take a bite and say, ugh, garlic.

1129
00:58:57.030 --> 00:59:00.490
Look, we had some fan questions about the foods.

1130
00:59:00.710 --> 00:59:05.610
Stacey and Rett V both wrote in to say, was any of that delicious looking buffet food real?

1131
00:59:06.030 --> 00:59:09.370
Did you get to sample some of the cuisine while filming this episode?

1132
00:59:09.610 --> 00:59:11.410
Guys, it was all real food.

1133
00:59:12.470 --> 00:59:13.570
It was all real.

1134
00:59:13.750 --> 00:59:14.610
It was all delicious.

1135
00:59:14.970 --> 00:59:21.110
Kent told me we hired a specialty food stylist to create the food, that it was authentically prepared.

1136
00:59:21.110 --> 00:59:24.750
And we had it all three days of filming and we got to eat it.

1137
00:59:24.890 --> 00:59:25.910
And I remember that.

1138
00:59:26.050 --> 00:59:26.850
It was delicious.

1139
00:59:27.250 --> 00:59:27.930
It was delicious.

1140
00:59:27.950 --> 00:59:30.750
I only got to eat the naan, but it was very good naan.

1141
00:59:31.470 --> 00:59:33.270
Oh, I ate between takes.

1142
00:59:33.790 --> 00:59:34.970
I just ate it.

1143
00:59:35.290 --> 00:59:37.610
You don't even see Pam eating it on screen.

1144
00:59:37.610 --> 00:59:39.050
I was like, I will eat this.

1145
00:59:39.290 --> 00:59:44.950
Well, now we come to one of the moments in this episode that is one of my favorites, Angela.

1146
00:59:45.270 --> 00:59:48.830
This is when Ryan meets Kelly's Giggly Sisters.

1147
00:59:49.270 --> 00:59:49.490
Yeah.

1148
00:59:50.230 --> 00:59:52.150
It's so, so cute.

1149
00:59:52.330 --> 01:00:01.650
We got some fan questions from Lindsay, Bridget, and Dan, who all want to know, do you know what Kelly's sister is saying when they're talking to Ryan?

1150
01:00:01.850 --> 01:00:03.890
They're saying something about Zach Braff.

1151
01:00:04.130 --> 01:00:04.370
Okay.

1152
01:00:04.410 --> 01:00:06.410
Here's what the three little girls say.

1153
01:00:06.630 --> 01:00:09.550
They say, Kelly likes Zach Braff.

1154
01:00:10.290 --> 01:00:12.390
That's what they're saying in Hindi.

1155
01:00:12.510 --> 01:00:13.910
And they're sort of like teasing him.

1156
01:00:13.910 --> 01:00:15.690
They were so cute.

1157
01:00:15.870 --> 01:00:20.330
And they were played by Tanvir Atwal, Ananya Keper, and Jaysha Patel.

1158
01:00:20.530 --> 01:00:26.790
Well, the little girl who plays Kelly's sister that says the Zach Braff line, that's Jaysha.

1159
01:00:26.790 --> 01:00:33.650
I found her on Instagram, and I reached out to her to ask her about what it was like to be on the show, and she wrote back.

1160
01:00:33.650 --> 01:00:34.970
I can't wait to share.

1161
01:00:35.210 --> 01:00:37.630
She must be like a grown lady now.

1162
01:00:37.870 --> 01:00:39.590
She is a grown woman now.

1163
01:00:39.590 --> 01:00:42.970
She told me she was 13 years old when she shot this episode.

1164
01:00:43.270 --> 01:00:46.190
She said she had not really heard about the show.

1165
01:00:46.530 --> 01:00:49.410
She was still watching Disney Channel, she said.

1166
01:00:49.590 --> 01:01:00.910
But she said her dad took her to the audition, and she remembers walking into the casting office and just seeing tons of other kids who were all there for the same role.

1167
01:01:01.090 --> 01:01:04.770
And she said the audition was just her saying that one line in Hindi.

1168
01:01:05.090 --> 01:01:07.230
And she said she didn't speak any Hindi.

1169
01:01:07.230 --> 01:01:14.150
So her dad told her how to say it about five seconds before she went into the audition room, and then she got the part.

1170
01:01:14.850 --> 01:01:23.430
So she said she was so excited, and I asked her what it was like to be on set, if she had any memories, and she sent back the sweetest message.

1171
01:01:23.430 --> 01:01:25.130
So we're going to play it for you now.

1172
01:01:25.630 --> 01:01:30.650
I remember Rainn Wilson walking up to me and shoving a lightsaber in my hand and yelling,

1173
01:01:30.810 --> 01:01:31.710
Lightsaber war!

1174
01:01:31.910 --> 01:01:36.830
I also remember getting to know Mindy Kaling and BJ Novak, who were so sweet to me.

1175
01:01:37.230 --> 01:01:44.530
Meeting Mindy Kaling really meant a lot to me growing up because I didn't really see many Indian actresses in the entertainment industry at that time.

1176
01:01:44.650 --> 01:01:50.190
And I love what Mindy has done with her platform, and she is still a huge inspiration for me till this day.

1177
01:01:50.190 --> 01:01:58.910
I also remember all of the delicious Indian food on set and getting to dance all day, and I remember being so happy that I had the chance to wear my Indian clothes.

1178
01:01:59.350 --> 01:02:00.590
Isn't that so sweet?

1179
01:02:00.710 --> 01:02:01.690
That is wonderful.

1180
01:02:02.230 --> 01:02:07.190
As I listened to it, I was just smiling so big because everything about that message is lovely.

1181
01:02:07.330 --> 01:02:08.450
I love all of her memories.

1182
01:02:08.650 --> 01:02:15.090
She's absolutely right about Mindy and what Mindy has done, and she's such an inspiration to so many people.

1183
01:02:16.070 --> 01:02:17.390
Yes, yeah.

1184
01:02:17.810 --> 01:02:27.270
She told me after the episode aired, she had classmates and family members reaching out that they had recorded it and taking pictures of her name in the credits.

1185
01:02:28.570 --> 01:02:30.570
So that was when she was 13.

1186
01:02:30.570 --> 01:02:31.930
She really wanted to be an actress.

1187
01:02:32.130 --> 01:02:36.570
She said when she was 15, she decided she wanted to go into journalism.

1188
01:02:36.570 --> 01:02:41.850
And now, Jaysha is the morning news reporter at NBC15 in Mobile, Alabama.

1189
01:02:42.370 --> 01:02:48.810
She told me she has to go to bed at 4 o'clock in the afternoon because she has to be in the studio at 3.30 in the morning.

1190
01:02:49.330 --> 01:02:56.430
I have always heard that about these morning anchors on the East Coast, that they have to get up so early.

1191
01:02:56.710 --> 01:02:58.390
That's amazing, though, Jaysha.

1192
01:02:58.630 --> 01:02:59.850
That is so cool.

1193
01:03:00.210 --> 01:03:01.210
Isn't that so cool?

1194
01:03:01.210 --> 01:03:08.130
She said all her co-workers know about her appearance on The Office and that fans will mention to her because she's Indian.

1195
01:03:08.670 --> 01:03:14.350
They'll mention the Diwali episode, and then she always, like, blows their mind when she says, oh, no, I was in it.

1196
01:03:14.730 --> 01:03:16.310
So I thought that was so sweet.

1197
01:03:16.570 --> 01:03:17.250
I was in it.

1198
01:03:17.330 --> 01:03:19.630
I say a line that offends Ryan the Temp.

1199
01:03:20.550 --> 01:03:21.510
Yes, exactly.

1200
01:03:21.790 --> 01:03:25.010
Except he doesn't quite know he's being the butt of a joke.

1201
01:03:25.270 --> 01:03:25.450
Right.

1202
01:03:25.450 --> 01:03:31.070
But she said being on The Office was one of her most memorable moments of her childhood.

1203
01:03:31.350 --> 01:03:36.190
I also love that, you know, I'm sure Rain improvised going up to her with that lightsaber.

1204
01:03:36.470 --> 01:03:40.510
There's a bunch of deleted scenes where he's fighting with kids with lightsabers.

1205
01:03:41.750 --> 01:03:43.130
And it didn't make it in.

1206
01:03:43.230 --> 01:03:47.930
But he, Rain looked very much in his element, like that's how he bonds with children.

1207
01:03:48.590 --> 01:03:48.930
Yes.

1208
01:03:49.190 --> 01:03:52.830
Angela, should we check in on those folks at Stanford, see how they're doing?

1209
01:03:52.830 --> 01:03:55.110
You mean the folks drinking Jägermeister?

1210
01:03:55.410 --> 01:03:55.630
Yeah.

1211
01:03:55.890 --> 01:03:56.590
How are they?

1212
01:03:56.910 --> 01:03:59.110
And Angela, did you see what they ordered for dinner?

1213
01:03:59.230 --> 01:04:01.030
Oh, Jenna, you and I know firsthand.

1214
01:04:01.890 --> 01:04:06.250
You do not drink a lot of alcohol and only eat sushi.

1215
01:04:06.630 --> 01:04:08.410
Now, Angela, why do we know that firsthand?

1216
01:04:08.410 --> 01:04:11.130
We know that because at the Golden Globes?

1217
01:04:11.210 --> 01:04:12.310
Was it the Golden Globes, Jenna?

1218
01:04:13.390 --> 01:04:17.110
Oh, lady, I was thinking of my bachelorette party that you planned for me.

1219
01:04:17.150 --> 01:04:19.330
Oh, well, there was the Golden Globes, but the bachelorette?

1220
01:04:19.550 --> 01:04:22.310
Wait, have we repeated this mistake multiple times?

1221
01:04:22.310 --> 01:04:24.870
Except the second time, I did better.

1222
01:04:25.030 --> 01:04:27.430
The first time, it did not work out well for me.

1223
01:04:27.550 --> 01:04:34.110
The second time, if memory serves, sorry to say this on here, but it hit your sister pretty hard.

1224
01:04:35.070 --> 01:04:35.610
Yeah.

1225
01:04:36.090 --> 01:04:40.630
Guys, Angela planned a bachelorette party for me when I was getting married to Lee,

1226
01:04:40.670 --> 01:04:43.770
and she took us all out for a sushi dinner.

1227
01:04:43.770 --> 01:04:51.250
It was a fancy-schmancy sushi place in Beverly Hills that I'd never eaten at, I'd only dreamed of.

1228
01:04:51.310 --> 01:04:54.470
And I was like, can we go there for my bachelorette?

1229
01:04:54.530 --> 01:04:56.390
They were thrilled to have us.

1230
01:04:56.530 --> 01:04:57.430
It was so cute.

1231
01:04:57.590 --> 01:04:59.470
All of the ladies from the office were there.

1232
01:04:59.650 --> 01:05:01.390
All of my other friends were there.

1233
01:05:01.390 --> 01:05:06.250
And afterwards, you took us to a dance club.

1234
01:05:06.590 --> 01:05:07.270
Hold up, lady.

1235
01:05:07.550 --> 01:05:08.950
We're going to get this right.

1236
01:05:09.190 --> 01:05:12.090
First of all, the sushi place was your idea.

1237
01:05:12.270 --> 01:05:16.350
And then after the sushi place, you guys, I got cupcakes with her face on it.

1238
01:05:16.430 --> 01:05:17.090
It was so cute.

1239
01:05:31.510 --> 01:05:33.430
And I was like, uh, what?

1240
01:05:34.690 --> 01:05:35.450
Wait, what?

1241
01:05:35.590 --> 01:05:35.930
Do you not?

1242
01:05:36.150 --> 01:05:36.910
Is this true?

1243
01:05:37.230 --> 01:05:38.390
I do not remember this.

1244
01:05:38.470 --> 01:05:38.570
Do you not know this?

1245
01:05:38.750 --> 01:05:39.110
No.

1246
01:05:39.410 --> 01:05:41.630
Lady, all I had planned was the dinner.

1247
01:05:41.870 --> 01:05:43.850
I didn't plan anything after.

1248
01:05:44.030 --> 01:05:46.190
Is this the first time you're ever hearing of this?

1249
01:05:47.030 --> 01:05:47.550
Yes.

1250
01:05:49.090 --> 01:05:55.430
This is putting the dance club into perspective now, because I thought at the time it was an

1251
01:05:55.430 --> 01:06:01.250
odd choice, because we've never in a million years gone clubbing, and now we were suddenly

1252
01:06:01.250 --> 01:06:02.790
clubbing for my bachelorette.

1253
01:06:02.870 --> 01:06:04.390
But I was like, this is great.

1254
01:06:04.570 --> 01:06:05.450
What a fun idea.

1255
01:06:05.690 --> 01:06:07.110
Yeah, I should say, you guys, we had a car.

1256
01:06:07.250 --> 01:06:10.370
I got one of the big limos, you know, that we could all pile in.

1257
01:06:10.490 --> 01:06:15.410
And I called a friend of mine who was like, always kind of like, got, you know, you have

1258
01:06:15.410 --> 01:06:16.930
that one friend that's like, I got a hookup.

1259
01:06:17.070 --> 01:06:17.670
I got a hookup.

1260
01:06:18.610 --> 01:06:19.710
Yeah, I'm in the know.

1261
01:06:19.970 --> 01:06:25.390
I called my friend Tess, and I was like, Tess, Jenna wants to go dancing.

1262
01:06:25.870 --> 01:06:27.310
We're in Beverly Hills.

1263
01:06:27.430 --> 01:06:27.810
What do I do?

1264
01:06:27.910 --> 01:06:28.330
What do I do?

1265
01:06:28.410 --> 01:06:29.470
And she was like, I'm on it.

1266
01:06:29.690 --> 01:06:31.050
Give me like five, 10 minutes.

1267
01:06:31.050 --> 01:06:31.730
I said, okay.

1268
01:06:32.470 --> 01:06:36.650
So we kind of hung out a little bit, and I was like, I'm sorting out some stuff, guys.

1269
01:06:36.770 --> 01:06:40.030
I do remember hanging out on the sidewalk outside the-

1270
01:06:40.030 --> 01:06:45.790
Yes, it's because I didn't have a plan, because all I had planned for was fancy sushi, and

1271
01:06:45.790 --> 01:06:48.090
our evening would have been over at like 10 o'clock.

1272
01:06:48.430 --> 01:06:48.710
Yeah.

1273
01:06:49.070 --> 01:06:54.490
Anyway, I get a call from Tess, and she goes, all right, Angela, it's pretty last minute.

1274
01:06:54.530 --> 01:06:57.530
It's like, you know, a Thursday night in Beverly Hills.

1275
01:06:57.710 --> 01:06:59.390
So I did get you in this one club.

1276
01:06:59.390 --> 01:07:00.390
I know this guy.

1277
01:07:00.550 --> 01:07:03.690
He's got a booth for you, and they're going to give you drink service.

1278
01:07:03.910 --> 01:07:06.030
It's kind of a random club, but it'll be fun.

1279
01:07:06.130 --> 01:07:07.130
You guys can dance.

1280
01:07:07.670 --> 01:07:11.730
Angela, it's the only time I've ever experienced bottle service.

1281
01:07:12.350 --> 01:07:18.530
Bottle service is where you like, they bring you just bottles of alcohol and then mixers

1282
01:07:18.530 --> 01:07:22.770
and like little cut limes to your table, and you make your drinks.

1283
01:07:22.770 --> 01:07:27.270
But also, when they walk it over, everyone starts doing, at least for us, I think this

1284
01:07:27.270 --> 01:07:30.130
was the norm, because I would see different people get bottle service, and it was like,

1285
01:07:30.350 --> 01:07:34.510
and they shut off like confetti in the air.

1286
01:07:34.610 --> 01:07:35.570
It was so weird.

1287
01:07:35.570 --> 01:07:36.930
It was so bizarre.

1288
01:07:37.210 --> 01:07:39.470
They had, it was crazy dancing.

1289
01:07:39.630 --> 01:07:44.330
I remember we got in trouble because we were dancing on top of the couches, and we got reprimanded

1290
01:07:44.330 --> 01:07:44.850
for that.

1291
01:07:45.450 --> 01:07:54.870
But guys, on our stomachs of sushi, mixed with bottle service, long story short, at the end

1292
01:07:54.870 --> 01:08:00.390
of the night, as the limo is dropping everyone off, my sister puked in Ellie Kemper's bushes.

1293
01:08:02.330 --> 01:08:04.210
I puked when I got home.

1294
01:08:04.390 --> 01:08:05.550
It was in my hair.

1295
01:08:05.770 --> 01:08:06.890
I slept in it.

1296
01:08:07.370 --> 01:08:09.070
It was an epic night.

1297
01:08:09.430 --> 01:08:13.290
But that's what you get when you mix sushi and a lot of booze.

1298
01:08:13.410 --> 01:08:16.010
And that is what is in store for these guys in Stanford.

1299
01:08:16.010 --> 01:08:20.890
Yeah, as Jenna and I re-watched this episode, I texted her and I was like, oh, lady, alcohol

1300
01:08:20.890 --> 01:08:21.590
and sushi.

1301
01:08:22.490 --> 01:08:23.670
It's so true.

1302
01:08:23.670 --> 01:08:25.650
It is so true.

1303
01:08:26.330 --> 01:08:32.010
Should we go back to Diwali because Roy has arrived and he is watching Pam dance and have

1304
01:08:32.010 --> 01:08:32.370
fun?

1305
01:08:32.830 --> 01:08:36.230
And I have a full Mindy catch for you right here.

1306
01:08:36.410 --> 01:08:38.830
And we've got a sting for it and everything.

1307
01:08:42.120 --> 01:08:43.240
There you go.

1308
01:08:43.440 --> 01:08:44.900
It's a full Mindy catch.

1309
01:08:45.380 --> 01:08:52.320
Mira During wrote in to say, at the Diwali party when Roy walks in, Beyonce's crazy in

1310
01:08:52.320 --> 01:08:54.260
Love is playing in the background.

1311
01:08:54.580 --> 01:08:57.440
And Angela, this was a note in the script.

1312
01:08:57.740 --> 01:09:03.400
Mindy wrote in what song would be playing when Roy walks in and that it would be a Beyonce

1313
01:09:03.400 --> 01:09:03.940
song.

1314
01:09:04.080 --> 01:09:07.360
So I think this is a full, full Mindy.

1315
01:09:07.360 --> 01:09:08.440
I love it.

1316
01:09:08.520 --> 01:09:10.500
It's a very subtle, full Mindy.

1317
01:09:10.680 --> 01:09:15.420
It's like full Mindy when you don't even see Mindy, but her presence is still there.

1318
01:09:15.840 --> 01:09:16.320
Exactly.

1319
01:09:16.800 --> 01:09:21.740
And, you know, my dance partner, we talked about this in the interview with Mindy.

1320
01:09:21.940 --> 01:09:26.640
My dance partner, Valli, okay, he was well known by the writers because he was a writer

1321
01:09:26.640 --> 01:09:28.460
on My Name is Earl at the time.

1322
01:09:29.040 --> 01:09:35.000
And he went on to write on 30 Rock and was one of the executive producers of Modern Family.

1323
01:09:35.140 --> 01:09:36.120
Oh, my gosh.

1324
01:09:37.000 --> 01:09:37.660
I know.

1325
01:09:37.900 --> 01:09:40.280
Well, Mindy did say, guys, he wasn't an actor.

1326
01:09:40.400 --> 01:09:41.600
He was like a friend of ours.

1327
01:09:43.120 --> 01:09:44.080
That's so wild.

1328
01:09:44.240 --> 01:09:47.600
Well, can I ask you a little bit about your dance moves there, Ms. Fisher?

1329
01:09:47.820 --> 01:09:48.360
You can.

1330
01:09:48.960 --> 01:09:50.060
What are you going to say?

1331
01:09:50.640 --> 01:09:51.820
I've danced with you.

1332
01:09:52.120 --> 01:09:56.620
And I can tell you right now, folks, that was not a choreographed dance routine.

1333
01:09:56.900 --> 01:09:58.620
That was just Jenna being Jenna.

1334
01:09:58.820 --> 01:09:59.060
Yeah.

1335
01:09:59.160 --> 01:10:02.560
We had a fan question from Zaria Collins who asked that same question.

1336
01:10:02.780 --> 01:10:05.340
Were those dance moves choreographed?

1337
01:10:05.420 --> 01:10:05.780
Oh, no.

1338
01:10:06.020 --> 01:10:06.360
Oh, no.

1339
01:10:06.540 --> 01:10:07.540
That's all Ms. Fisher.

1340
01:10:07.900 --> 01:10:11.540
That's me fully dancing with my heart and soul.

1341
01:10:11.740 --> 01:10:13.440
That's hello, St. Louis.

1342
01:10:14.880 --> 01:10:16.020
St. Louis prom.

1343
01:10:16.460 --> 01:10:17.600
That sounds of Scranton right there.

1344
01:10:17.600 --> 01:10:22.220
That's the same girl who made a Sounds of Scranton playlist, everyone.

1345
01:10:22.760 --> 01:10:23.840
There I am.

1346
01:10:24.040 --> 01:10:27.420
You could almost rewind me and put me in my high school gym right there.

1347
01:10:27.680 --> 01:10:34.040
Well, something is going to happen that is super awkward because that is Michael's way.

1348
01:10:34.980 --> 01:10:40.000
Michael's way is to take a wonderful moment and make everyone cringe.

1349
01:10:40.420 --> 01:10:43.440
And the Diwali was going to be no exception.

1350
01:10:44.180 --> 01:10:51.120
He, you know, has this amazing scene with Mindy's parents that play Kelly's parents, which we already talked about.

1351
01:10:51.420 --> 01:10:54.480
And he's so inspired by their love.

1352
01:10:55.100 --> 01:10:56.180
He's going to do it.

1353
01:10:56.240 --> 01:10:56.380
Yeah.

1354
01:10:56.560 --> 01:10:57.400
He's going to do it.

1355
01:10:57.520 --> 01:10:58.180
Their commitment.

1356
01:10:58.600 --> 01:10:59.060
Yeah.

1357
01:10:59.220 --> 01:11:06.780
He's going to propose to Carol in front of a whole room of strangers on their ninth date.

1358
01:11:07.720 --> 01:11:16.060
And she's like, Carol, will you do me the honor of making me your husband, of making me your husband?

1359
01:11:16.180 --> 01:11:19.580
And she's like, can we talk about this in private?

1360
01:11:19.920 --> 01:11:24.700
And this is one of my favorite moments in movies and TV where he's like, what?

1361
01:11:24.860 --> 01:11:25.680
Into a microphone.

1362
01:11:25.860 --> 01:11:29.200
She's like, can we talk about it in private?

1363
01:11:30.620 --> 01:11:33.020
And then he's like, oh, man, oh, crap.

1364
01:11:34.840 --> 01:11:43.220
Well, they have this scene out in the parking lot, Jenna, and it made me laugh so hard that, you know, Carol is like, I can't do this, Michael.

1365
01:11:43.300 --> 01:11:43.860
I can't do it.

1366
01:11:43.980 --> 01:11:50.900
And his last ditch effort, his last few moments, what is he going to say that might change her mind?

1367
01:11:51.060 --> 01:11:52.300
He's going to go for it.

1368
01:11:52.400 --> 01:11:55.400
What could he say to change this woman's mind?

1369
01:11:55.740 --> 01:11:56.640
Do you know what he says?

1370
01:11:56.860 --> 01:11:57.980
Let me come with you.

1371
01:11:57.980 --> 01:12:00.680
I have this book, the Kama Sutra.

1372
01:12:04.000 --> 01:12:07.020
She says, she's like, good night, Michael.

1373
01:12:07.500 --> 01:12:15.320
Well, at this point, Pam is, she's talking to Valley and she's realizing something.

1374
01:12:15.780 --> 01:12:17.620
She wants to reach out to Jim.

1375
01:12:18.120 --> 01:12:20.560
So she's going to, she's going to text Jim.

1376
01:12:20.660 --> 01:12:21.320
Well, that thing happened.

1377
01:12:21.560 --> 01:12:26.460
That thing happened, which is, you know, this, this crazy moment just happened.

1378
01:12:26.700 --> 01:12:28.380
And who does she want to share it with?

1379
01:12:28.620 --> 01:12:29.080
Right?

1380
01:12:29.660 --> 01:12:32.400
This is how you know you really care about someone.

1381
01:12:32.840 --> 01:12:38.120
Your person out there, folks, is the person you want to tell everything to right after it happens.

1382
01:12:38.400 --> 01:12:40.580
It's who you bounce everything off of.

1383
01:12:40.840 --> 01:12:44.580
And Pam wants to tell her person what just happened.

1384
01:12:46.120 --> 01:12:47.620
But she runs into Angela.

1385
01:12:47.820 --> 01:12:47.920
Oh.

1386
01:12:49.320 --> 01:12:51.060
She needs to get her shoes.

1387
01:12:51.440 --> 01:12:54.880
And there is Angela guarding the shoes, she says.

1388
01:12:54.900 --> 01:12:57.040
Well, and eating her dry naan.

1389
01:12:57.360 --> 01:12:59.680
By the way, Angela, fan question from Rainy Greg.

1390
01:12:59.880 --> 01:13:00.780
Was the naan dry?

1391
01:13:01.420 --> 01:13:01.780
No.

1392
01:13:02.300 --> 01:13:03.380
Was it actually dry?

1393
01:13:03.620 --> 01:13:03.940
No, it wasn't.

1394
01:13:04.080 --> 01:13:05.500
It was perfectly fine.

1395
01:13:05.500 --> 01:13:07.740
I would say that, too.

1396
01:13:07.820 --> 01:13:08.480
I ate some of that naan.

1397
01:13:08.480 --> 01:13:09.000
It was wonderful.

1398
01:13:09.280 --> 01:13:10.220
I was glad to have it.

1399
01:13:10.420 --> 01:13:11.560
I was probably hungry.

1400
01:13:12.040 --> 01:13:17.300
Well, Jen and I used to always get so tickled to have scenes together because it rarely happened.

1401
01:13:17.300 --> 01:13:19.920
And so we were really excited about this.

1402
01:13:20.120 --> 01:13:22.320
I loved shooting this scene with you.

1403
01:13:22.460 --> 01:13:23.700
And I love it so much.

1404
01:13:23.720 --> 01:13:25.000
I just want us to play it.

1405
01:13:25.140 --> 01:13:26.060
Sam, can you play it?

1406
01:13:27.260 --> 01:13:28.160
It's hot in there.

1407
01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:30.880
How's the naan?

1408
01:13:31.260 --> 01:13:31.680
Dry.

1409
01:13:32.580 --> 01:13:33.900
Looked like you were having fun.

1410
01:13:34.480 --> 01:13:35.140
I am.

1411
01:13:35.360 --> 01:13:36.540
You should come dance with us.

1412
01:13:36.800 --> 01:13:39.060
I have to watch our shoes so they don't get stolen.

1413
01:13:39.700 --> 01:13:40.660
Who are you texting?

1414
01:13:41.120 --> 01:13:41.640
No one.

1415
01:13:42.680 --> 01:13:42.920
Aw.

1416
01:13:43.140 --> 01:13:47.340
But also, lady, my character is so nosy.

1417
01:13:48.360 --> 01:13:49.080
So nosy?

1418
01:13:49.160 --> 01:13:49.640
Who are you texting?

1419
01:13:49.660 --> 01:13:50.640
Yeah, looked like you were having fun.

1420
01:13:50.660 --> 01:13:51.260
Who are you texting?

1421
01:13:51.460 --> 01:13:54.300
I mean, who am I to ask you who you're texting?

1422
01:13:55.360 --> 01:13:56.700
You're the party police.

1423
01:13:56.700 --> 01:13:58.460
Also, you're single.

1424
01:13:58.820 --> 01:14:01.080
Dwight made this big announcement that he's single.

1425
01:14:01.320 --> 01:14:02.040
I don't know.

1426
01:14:02.200 --> 01:14:03.300
Maybe you're texting Dwight.

1427
01:14:03.480 --> 01:14:04.000
What's happening?

1428
01:14:04.480 --> 01:14:05.960
Angela's spinning out in this episode.

1429
01:14:06.180 --> 01:14:08.120
And a lot of those scenes ended up getting deleted.

1430
01:14:08.120 --> 01:14:14.220
But it would be a fun watch to go back and watch them because that is why you are so intense in this episode.

1431
01:14:14.660 --> 01:14:17.780
So now Pam is going to make it outside.

1432
01:14:18.080 --> 01:14:20.960
She hasn't received a text back from Jim.

1433
01:14:21.400 --> 01:14:23.180
And she sits with Michael.

1434
01:14:23.980 --> 01:14:25.520
Michael tries to relate to her.

1435
01:14:25.520 --> 01:14:28.320
He's like, wow, they're both victims of broken engagements.

1436
01:14:28.820 --> 01:14:34.320
And Pam's like, well, I mean, except that you were never actually engaged, but whatever.

1437
01:14:34.600 --> 01:14:36.300
She tries to bond with Michael.

1438
01:14:36.300 --> 01:14:43.000
And, of course, he does that thing that you were just talking about where he just takes it one step too far.

1439
01:14:43.280 --> 01:14:46.980
And he starts to lean in like he's going to kiss her.

1440
01:14:47.240 --> 01:14:48.360
So awkward.

1441
01:14:48.360 --> 01:14:50.880
We got a lot of mail about it, Angela.

1442
01:14:51.440 --> 01:15:00.020
Ruby, Alexandra, and Vanessa Ortiz all wrote in to ask if that was a scripted moment when Michael tries to kiss Pam.

1443
01:15:00.020 --> 01:15:02.420
Pam, what was it like?

1444
01:15:02.700 --> 01:15:04.520
It was scripted, you guys.

1445
01:15:04.720 --> 01:15:05.920
That was in the script.

1446
01:15:06.000 --> 01:15:12.360
And then the thing, that great line that Pam has where she says, I'm rejecting your kiss.

1447
01:15:12.500 --> 01:15:14.040
He's like, she's like, what are you doing?

1448
01:15:14.100 --> 01:15:14.820
He's like, what are you doing?

1449
01:15:14.920 --> 01:15:16.820
She's like, I'm rejecting your kiss.

1450
01:15:16.980 --> 01:15:17.940
That's what I'm doing.

1451
01:15:17.940 --> 01:15:20.120
Yeah, what are you doing?

1452
01:15:20.360 --> 01:15:21.840
That was all scripted.

1453
01:15:21.960 --> 01:15:29.620
And, Angela, I was so excited to do that scene because I remember staying late that evening and shooting outside.

1454
01:15:30.040 --> 01:15:37.440
I talked about this before when I had that scene with John up on the roof where Pam and Jim eat the grilled cheese sandwiches.

1455
01:15:37.440 --> 01:15:41.080
It was one of those warm summer evenings in Los Angeles.

1456
01:15:41.080 --> 01:15:42.040
They're the beSt.

1457
01:15:42.380 --> 01:15:44.200
This was another one of those.

1458
01:15:44.200 --> 01:15:53.420
And it's one of my fondest memories from shooting the show because I got Steve all to myself, and I got Miguel Arteta all to myself, and Mindy was there,

1459
01:15:53.560 --> 01:15:57.860
and it was just us doing this scene, getting it just perfect.

1460
01:15:57.860 --> 01:16:00.000
It felt like we had all the time in the world.

1461
01:16:00.000 --> 01:16:01.240
There was no rush.

1462
01:16:01.600 --> 01:16:04.520
And, oh, I just absolutely loved it.

1463
01:16:04.820 --> 01:16:12.920
Yeah, well, Mindy mentioned, you know, that she was kind of jealous of her parents that they got to have this great scene with Steve because there are several characters,

1464
01:16:13.160 --> 01:16:13.820
myself included,

1465
01:16:13.820 --> 01:16:16.720
that rarely got to have one-on-one scenes with Steve.

1466
01:16:16.880 --> 01:16:19.000
It just wouldn't make sense in the world of the show.

1467
01:16:19.180 --> 01:16:22.660
And whenever I did, it felt so special.

1468
01:16:22.880 --> 01:16:28.140
And I think you got to have some amazing scenes with him throughout the course of the show,

1469
01:16:28.140 --> 01:16:36.020
and this is just one of those that was just beautiful and so fun and funny and cringy and heartfelt, just all of it.

1470
01:16:36.140 --> 01:16:36.760
That's all true.

1471
01:16:36.940 --> 01:16:41.600
Angela, we did have someone write in with an old tech alert that I thought you would appreciate.

1472
01:16:41.600 --> 01:16:42.160
Hit me up.

1473
01:16:42.200 --> 01:16:42.900
How did I miss it?

1474
01:16:42.900 --> 01:16:43.440
What is it?

1475
01:16:43.580 --> 01:16:53.260
Kayla Whitehead said Pam's cell phone is such old tech, but she's like, but also, when she walks outside, Michael sees her on the steps,

1476
01:16:53.260 --> 01:16:57.320
and he notices that she's holding her phone, and he says, expecting a call.

1477
01:16:57.760 --> 01:17:00.240
She was like, no one would say that to you today.

1478
01:17:00.300 --> 01:17:06.400
If you have your phone in your hand today, no one's, like, expecting a call because we always all have our phones in our hands.

1479
01:17:06.520 --> 01:17:08.620
That is a brilliant catch.

1480
01:17:08.680 --> 01:17:11.060
I am applauding that catch.

1481
01:17:11.060 --> 01:17:12.640
I love that observation.

1482
01:17:13.000 --> 01:17:16.920
That is an amazing observation because back then, yeah, your phone was in your purse.

1483
01:17:17.080 --> 01:17:22.960
It was, we didn't walk around holding phones, like flip phones like that, because we did hardly anything with them other than talk to someone.

1484
01:17:23.000 --> 01:17:26.520
So if you're holding it, you'd probably just spoke to someone or you were about to.

1485
01:17:26.520 --> 01:17:28.580
Yes, that is a great observation.

1486
01:17:28.800 --> 01:17:29.020
Pretty great.

1487
01:17:29.020 --> 01:17:39.420
Well, I want to take us back to Stanford because I think there is a moment in this episode that is the happiest we have seen Andy since he has appeared on the show.

1488
01:17:39.860 --> 01:17:41.220
It's Happy Andy.

1489
01:17:41.640 --> 01:17:45.240
And I want to talk, I want to share Happy Andy with you.

1490
01:17:45.920 --> 01:17:48.260
Happy Andy happens at around 15 minutes.

1491
01:17:48.260 --> 01:17:51.140
It's, they have had a lot of Jaeger.

1492
01:17:51.640 --> 01:17:55.700
Karen, though, she's just tossing her Jaeger shots into the trash.

1493
01:17:55.980 --> 01:17:57.160
No one knows it.

1494
01:17:57.440 --> 01:17:58.920
She's not getting wasted.

1495
01:17:59.680 --> 01:18:02.380
And Andy starts singing acapella.

1496
01:18:02.540 --> 01:18:04.120
Karen's like, no acapella, Andy.

1497
01:18:04.300 --> 01:18:08.280
But he's drunk and he's singing the Indigo Girls Closer to Fine.

1498
01:18:08.280 --> 01:18:15.220
And as he drunkenly sings, all of a sudden, Jim, who's super wasted, starts joining in and singing.

1499
01:18:15.480 --> 01:18:18.020
And it's so adorable.

1500
01:18:18.280 --> 01:18:19.760
Andy's like, Tuna!

1501
01:18:19.760 --> 01:18:21.340
Are you kidding me?

1502
01:18:21.540 --> 01:18:24.860
Like, he's so happy.

1503
01:18:25.140 --> 01:18:26.100
He's so happy.

1504
01:18:26.240 --> 01:18:28.100
They're having like an acapella moment.

1505
01:18:28.300 --> 01:18:30.280
And this is Happy Andy.

1506
01:18:30.500 --> 01:18:31.300
He is thrilled.

1507
01:18:31.600 --> 01:18:36.340
Well, Angela, we had a fan catch from Renata Torres.

1508
01:18:36.920 --> 01:18:44.280
She says at 17 minutes, 58 seconds, you can see a pair of white flip-flops under Karen's desk.

1509
01:18:44.340 --> 01:18:44.620
Ah!

1510
01:18:45.100 --> 01:18:49.140
And she wanted to know if that was on purpose, but we know why those are there.

1511
01:18:49.400 --> 01:18:50.060
We do.

1512
01:18:50.240 --> 01:18:51.760
Those were Rashida's flip-flops.

1513
01:18:51.980 --> 01:18:59.360
Yeah, the wardrobe department would give us Uggs or flip-flops to wear to and from our trailers and set

1514
01:18:59.360 --> 01:19:04.020
so we didn't have to walk in our kind of like high-heel office shoes, right?

1515
01:19:04.160 --> 01:19:04.480
Yes.

1516
01:19:05.200 --> 01:19:05.640
Yes!

1517
01:19:06.000 --> 01:19:08.880
You caught Rashida's flip-flops.

1518
01:19:09.100 --> 01:19:15.040
You know, wardrobe actually told me one time also, our trailers were not close to the soundstage.

1519
01:19:15.160 --> 01:19:16.720
It was a little, you know, quite a walk.

1520
01:19:16.860 --> 01:19:20.540
And they said that also they would take our shoes to protect our shoes.

1521
01:19:20.760 --> 01:19:26.060
Because if we walked across the parking lot back and forth, and sometimes if there was weather of any kind,

1522
01:19:26.060 --> 01:19:34.080
they preferred actually to leave our shoes on set by our desks rather than us walking around in them all the time.

1523
01:19:34.220 --> 01:19:36.580
And we were delighted because that meant less time in heels.

1524
01:19:36.580 --> 01:19:38.160
We had our travel shoes.

1525
01:19:38.380 --> 01:19:40.400
Those were Rashida's travel shoes.

1526
01:19:40.960 --> 01:19:46.960
Well, as they're leaving for the night in Stanford, Jim is going to ride that bike home.

1527
01:19:47.140 --> 01:19:48.720
He's going to ride his bike home.

1528
01:19:48.840 --> 01:19:49.820
Or is he?

1529
01:19:49.900 --> 01:19:50.480
Well, yeah.

1530
01:19:50.700 --> 01:19:51.680
He falls over.

1531
01:19:51.680 --> 01:19:53.960
Well, you know, it's the end of the night at Stanford.

1532
01:19:53.980 --> 01:19:54.940
They've had Jaeger.

1533
01:19:55.200 --> 01:19:56.960
They've bonded over Indigo Girls.

1534
01:19:57.540 --> 01:20:00.080
I mean, Andy's busting out his air mattress.

1535
01:20:00.420 --> 01:20:01.220
He's like...

1536
01:20:01.220 --> 01:20:01.680
Oh, yeah.

1537
01:20:01.920 --> 01:20:03.580
He's staying in for the night.

1538
01:20:04.120 --> 01:20:08.120
Jim is going to try to ride his giant bicycle with the big basket home.

1539
01:20:08.120 --> 01:20:11.140
And he, like, tips over into the bushes.

1540
01:20:11.140 --> 01:20:13.460
And Karen's in her car.

1541
01:20:13.460 --> 01:20:14.620
She's like, hold up.

1542
01:20:14.780 --> 01:20:16.240
Get in my car, drunky.

1543
01:20:16.940 --> 01:20:21.020
And, Jenna, do you remember how freaked out people were about this moment?

1544
01:20:22.380 --> 01:20:22.820
Yeah.

1545
01:20:23.040 --> 01:20:28.420
I mean, people thought Karen was shady, that she let them get so wasted, and that...

1546
01:20:28.420 --> 01:20:30.240
Was she waiting for Jim?

1547
01:20:30.240 --> 01:20:31.660
Like she had planned it all along.

1548
01:20:31.660 --> 01:20:33.840
Yeah, was she waiting out in the parking lot for Jim?

1549
01:20:33.840 --> 01:20:36.140
I was like, hey, Mr. Tipsy, get in my car.

1550
01:20:36.140 --> 01:20:41.180
And remember, in this episode, it was written that they were going to, like, kiss.

1551
01:20:41.580 --> 01:20:43.020
Oh, I talked to Rashida about it.

1552
01:20:43.080 --> 01:20:46.720
I texted with her, and I want to read you guys what she said.

1553
01:20:46.880 --> 01:20:53.580
She said, in this episode, they had written a scene where Jim and Karen get sloppy drunk and make out.

1554
01:20:53.760 --> 01:20:57.760
So maybe, I guess, she had been drinking, too, in that different version, right?

1555
01:20:58.240 --> 01:21:02.220
In that different version, because I have the scripted version of that,

1556
01:21:02.220 --> 01:21:07.160
that they, the three of them go to a bar, and they all get drunk together at a bar.

1557
01:21:07.380 --> 01:21:11.260
And then they were supposed to make out on the street outside of this bar.

1558
01:21:11.440 --> 01:21:11.540
Yeah.

1559
01:21:11.960 --> 01:21:16.760
And Rashida said they actually filmed the scene in the parking lot.

1560
01:21:17.820 --> 01:21:18.520
Oh, my God.

1561
01:21:18.800 --> 01:21:21.080
And she said she was really worried.

1562
01:21:21.240 --> 01:21:22.380
She was like, everyone's going to hate me.

1563
01:21:22.380 --> 01:21:27.640
And then she told me Stephen Merchant actually suggested that they cut the scene out.

1564
01:21:28.420 --> 01:21:29.960
That he got to watch a verse.

1565
01:21:30.060 --> 01:21:34.960
Because Stephen and Ricky would watch our episodes, and they would give the producers notes.

1566
01:21:35.580 --> 01:21:36.820
Rarely, but sometimes.

1567
01:21:37.080 --> 01:21:39.360
And their notes were always correct.

1568
01:21:39.700 --> 01:21:42.980
They were always like, they knew, don't move that needle so far.

1569
01:21:42.980 --> 01:21:47.240
Yeah, and Rashida said she felt like Stephen really understood the relationships.

1570
01:21:47.960 --> 01:21:51.260
And that this was going too far, too bold, too quickly.

1571
01:21:51.660 --> 01:21:55.120
And it would sort of sabotage anything that Jim and Karen might,

1572
01:21:55.500 --> 01:21:57.720
could possibly be as a foil for Pam.

1573
01:21:57.860 --> 01:21:58.740
It was just too much.

1574
01:21:58.940 --> 01:22:03.580
Yeah, I think if you wanted to believe in their relationship, which you will,

1575
01:22:03.980 --> 01:22:07.200
like Jim and Karen are going to really have a great relationship.

1576
01:22:07.380 --> 01:22:11.340
You don't want it to start off with like a sloppy drunk make out.

1577
01:22:11.340 --> 01:22:12.820
On the side of the street.

1578
01:22:13.160 --> 01:22:13.960
Kids, are you listening?

1579
01:22:14.140 --> 01:22:15.560
Nothing good happens after midnight.

1580
01:22:15.880 --> 01:22:16.760
Okay, go home.

1581
01:22:17.140 --> 01:22:19.000
This is what my aunt told me when I went off to college.

1582
01:22:19.240 --> 01:22:23.020
She said, here's my advice to you about sleeping around.

1583
01:22:23.300 --> 01:22:24.380
This is what she said.

1584
01:22:24.800 --> 01:22:26.720
She said, you're going to go to these parties.

1585
01:22:27.140 --> 01:22:28.460
You're going to do some drinking.

1586
01:22:28.840 --> 01:22:32.800
And you might, in the moment, want to make a decision that's impulsive.

1587
01:22:33.140 --> 01:22:35.660
She said, my advice to you is go home.

1588
01:22:36.280 --> 01:22:39.160
Because you can always wake up in the morning and say,

1589
01:22:39.280 --> 01:22:41.060
oh, I wish I'd slept with that guy.

1590
01:22:41.340 --> 01:22:43.100
And you can do something about it.

1591
01:22:43.360 --> 01:22:44.800
But you can't undo.

1592
01:22:45.220 --> 01:22:46.320
You can't undo.

1593
01:22:47.160 --> 01:22:48.600
Yeah, I'm with your aunt.

1594
01:22:48.860 --> 01:22:50.040
You can't undo.

1595
01:22:50.340 --> 01:22:52.240
But I was kind of lame in college.

1596
01:22:52.460 --> 01:22:58.820
When I turned 21, I had a big paper due for a class I was taking.

1597
01:22:59.920 --> 01:23:01.920
And all my friends were like, you're going to go out.

1598
01:23:02.080 --> 01:23:02.880
It's your 21st birthday.

1599
01:23:03.300 --> 01:23:05.500
And I said, oh, no, I need to work on my paper.

1600
01:23:05.500 --> 01:23:06.800
So I worked on my paper.

1601
01:23:07.000 --> 01:23:09.700
And my dad had a Texaco gas card.

1602
01:23:09.700 --> 01:23:11.960
And he would pay my Texaco gas card.

1603
01:23:12.480 --> 01:23:15.680
Just like Reality Bites, I would go to that gas station.

1604
01:23:15.720 --> 01:23:21.000
And I would get gas, bread, sandwich, meat, potato chips, soda, like everything.

1605
01:23:21.000 --> 01:23:24.260
And I went to Texaco.

1606
01:23:24.260 --> 01:23:27.040
And I bought myself a Coronita.

1607
01:23:27.680 --> 01:23:29.420
It's not even the big Corona.

1608
01:23:29.700 --> 01:23:30.940
It's a Coronita.

1609
01:23:31.580 --> 01:23:32.980
Because I was 21.

1610
01:23:33.400 --> 01:23:35.840
And I went and I worked on my term paper.

1611
01:23:35.980 --> 01:23:37.320
And I had my Coronita.

1612
01:23:37.480 --> 01:23:39.040
And that was my 21st birthday.

1613
01:23:39.980 --> 01:23:41.380
That is literally adorable.

1614
01:23:43.020 --> 01:23:43.860
That is adorable.

1615
01:23:44.060 --> 01:23:45.080
I was a big dork lady.

1616
01:23:45.280 --> 01:23:46.360
That's why we would have been friends.

1617
01:23:46.440 --> 01:23:48.160
I would have hung out with you and your cat.

1618
01:23:48.380 --> 01:23:49.320
We would have been besties.

1619
01:23:50.060 --> 01:23:55.100
This is also why, as adults, we mixed sushi with a lot of hard liquor.

1620
01:23:55.180 --> 01:23:56.740
Because we didn't learn in college.

1621
01:23:56.740 --> 01:23:57.480
We didn't learn.

1622
01:23:57.600 --> 01:23:58.260
Where are we at?

1623
01:23:58.260 --> 01:23:59.460
I don't even know where we're at.

1624
01:23:59.500 --> 01:24:01.260
Except that Karen put Jim in his car.

1625
01:24:01.520 --> 01:24:03.240
And now we go back to Diwali.

1626
01:24:03.440 --> 01:24:05.300
And it's one of my favorite moments ever.

1627
01:24:05.940 --> 01:24:10.540
Dwight and Michael are going to perform a cover of Adam Sandler's Hanukkah song.

1628
01:24:11.400 --> 01:24:13.120
Dedicated to Indians everywhere.

1629
01:24:14.360 --> 01:24:16.300
Yes, the crowd loves it.

1630
01:24:16.740 --> 01:24:20.260
Angela, so many people wrote in asking about this song.

1631
01:24:20.400 --> 01:24:21.440
Was it improvised?

1632
01:24:21.660 --> 01:24:26.680
A lot of people thought that because Steve was holding a piece of paper that maybe we wrote this on the fly.

1633
01:24:27.000 --> 01:24:29.360
No, this was in the script.

1634
01:24:29.360 --> 01:24:35.440
And in fact, Kent told me it had been in the script as far back as the pre-table draft.

1635
01:24:35.800 --> 01:24:37.520
This is kind of a writer's term.

1636
01:24:37.660 --> 01:24:41.400
But they send out a draft of the script before they let anyone see it.

1637
01:24:41.480 --> 01:24:47.740
And they have to give it to all of the main producers so that they can start planning wardrobe and locations.

1638
01:24:48.160 --> 01:24:53.060
And Kent said that at that pre-table draft, this was the tag for the episode.

1639
01:24:53.060 --> 01:24:55.680
And it remained there until we shot it.

1640
01:24:55.680 --> 01:24:58.520
So they got permission and all that kind of stuff.

